From: j7
Subject: j7: raise the GPU PLL on every boot, not only when the clock dump is asked for

0397 changed the j7gpuclk default to 900 MHz, but the whole CMU_G3D block - the readback, the
M/P/S write, the log line - sits inside the j7clk gate, and j7clk dumps CMU_MIF and is off by
default.  On a cmdline without j7clk=1 the GPU PLL was never touched, so the "900 MHz by default"
image still ran the GPU at the bootloader's 343 MHz: the change was dead code.

Move the CMU_G3D block out of the gate so it runs at every boot, keep CMU_MIF behind j7clk as
before, and leave the rest of the sequence alone: 900 MHz is the rate the 0374 boot read back on
this phone, j7gpuclk=0 keeps the bootloader rate, and the register is read back and decoded.  The
GPU is a separate clock domain, so this cannot take the CPU with it the way the ARMCLK move did.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

